mapping "Q878B.1" source="Q878B" target="5619004" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target quality=100 {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source Q878B SNOMED CT 5619004 = Laurence-Moon-Biedl syndrome (Swedish clinical usage bundles
        Laurence-Moon and Bardet-Biedl, which SNOMED CT separates). Target (concept_id 4209284) =
        Bardet-Biedl syndrome, standard=S; this is the active standard concept that the deprecated
        SNOMED CT 232060005 (concept_id 40436251) Maps to per mirror relationship. Target is broader in the
        clinical sense that Bardet-Biedl is now the preferred term for the BBS phenotype; the Swedish
        source uses the historical combined name. : crosswalk-verified to the standard concept, small
        breadth mismatch from the historical lumping.
        """
}
mapping "Q878C.1" source="Q878C" target="57838006" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source Q878C SNOMED CT 57838006 = Usher syndrome (retinitis pigmentosa with progressive
        sensorineural hearing loss). No generic SNOMED CT concept exists in the mirror — only the
        type-specific descendants 232057003 (type 1), 232058008 (type 2) and the type-1F descendant
        514793471000119104. The closest standard ancestor that fully subsumes all Usher types is
        (concept_id 4240613) = Retinitis pigmentosa-deafness syndrome, standard=S; ancestor of both
        Usher type 1 and type 2 per the SNOMED CT ancestor table. : target legitimately subsumes the
        source, but is a coarser category (broader) and there is no exact generic concept.
        """
}
